cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "HLA class I engageability: a sequence-derived axis of immune potency and a reproducible HLA-LOH escape finding"
authors:
  - family-names: Nadler
    given-names: Rebecca
    affiliation: "Weill Cornell / Memorial Sloan Kettering / Rockefeller (MD-PhD)"
date-released: 2026-07-13
license: MIT
keywords:
  - HLA class I
  - engageability
  - TCR recognition
  - HLA loss of heterozygosity
  - immune escape
  - antigen presentation
  - immunotherapy
abstract: >
  A sequence-derived, HED-orthogonal metric of HLA class I "engageability" (TCR-facing
  surface permissiveness), a multi-axis decomposition of immunogenic potency, an
  identifiability analysis of allele-level ICB outcome associations, and a reproducible
  somatic finding: a locus-wide HLA-B loss/retention hierarchy under HLA-LOH with
  HLA-B*58:01 preferentially lost. Built for the Claude Science Hackathon 2026 (research track).
